    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Quillsen are delighted to present No. 52 Sandford Road to the market, a distinguished period residence of exceptional character and scale occupying a prime position in the heart of Dublin 6.\n\nIn need of some modernisation viewing is strongly recommended.\n\nOccupying an elevated position on this highly regarded and sought-after residential road, No. 52 is a handsome three-storey Victorian residence extending to approximately 240 sq.m. / 2,583 sq.ft. Rich in architectural heritage and retaining some original period features, this fine home offers the rare opportunity to acquire a substantial family residence in one of Dublin`s most desirable locations.\n\nBehind its attractive red-brick façade, granite steps and distinctive entrance lies a home of immense warmth, elegance and character. Throughout the property, some original features remain beautifully intact including ornate plasterwork, ceiling coving, decorative centre roses, original fireplaces and timber flooring. Newly fitted sash windows flood the accommodation with natural light.\n\nThe gracious proportions synonymous with homes of this era are immediately evident upon entering the impressive reception hall. The accommodation is exceptionally versatile and extends over several levels, offering an ideal balance between formal reception rooms and practical family living spaces.\n\nParticularly impressive are the elegant reception rooms which enjoy magnificent ceiling heights and large picture sash windows overlooking Sandford Road and the landmark St. Mary`s Church opposite. These wonderful rooms provide a rare sense of space and grandeur while perfectly showcasing period detailing.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an impressive entrance hall, drawing room, living room, family room, dining area, kitchen, five bedrooms and a top-floor suite.\n\nAt garden level, the kitchen, dining area and family room combine to create an inviting heart to the home, ideal for everyday family life.\n\nOutside, the property benefits from valuable gated off-street parking to the front, a particularly sought-after feature in this mature residential setting. To the rear is a private walled garden providing a peaceful and secluded outdoor space requiring minimal maintenance.\n\nThe location is second to none. Sandford Road enjoys a highly convenient position between Ranelagh, Donnybrook and Ballsbridge, with a wealth of amenities within easy walking distance. Ranelagh Village offers an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, speciality shops and neighbourhood services, while the LUAS provides swift access to St. Stephen`s Green and the city centre.\n\nThe area is particularly well served by many of Dublin`s most highly regarded primary and secondary schools together with UCD, Trinity College Dublin and an abundance of sporting and recreational amenities. Herbert Park, Fitzwilliam Lawn Tennis Club, the Aviva Stadium and the city centre are all within easy reach.\n\nRarely does a protected period residence of such scale, character and convenience come to the market in this prime Dublin 6 location. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Garden Level\n\nEntrance\nEntrance Lobby with tiled floor and understairs storage.\n\nFamily Room - 6.47m (21'3\") x 3.97m (13'0\")\nSpacious family room with tiled floor providing a comfortable and versatile living space adjacent to the kitchen.\n\nKitchen - 4.59m (15'1\") x 3.97m (13'0\")\nWell-appointed kitchen with extensive storage and ample worktop space forming the heart of the home. Tiled floor. Door to bedroom.\n\nBedroom - 3.79m (12'5\") x 4.86m (15'11\")\nDoor to shower room/utility room. Door to rear garden.\n\nSpacious shower room/utility room - 3.68m (12'1\") x 3.98m (13'1\")\nTiled shower, wc & whb. Plumbed for washing machine.\n\nHall Level\n\nEntrance Hallway\nImpressive reception hallway featuring original timber flooring, ornate ceiling coving, 2 built-in display units, decorative archway and magnificent ceiling heights.\n\nDrawing Room - 4.59m (15'1\") x 3.91m (12'10\")\nElegant formal reception room to the front with large sash window, feature fireplace with cast iron inset & marble hearth, exposed varnished floorboards intricate cornicing and attractive views across Sandford Road. Double doors to living room.\n\nLiving Room - 4.59m (15'1\") x 4.16m (13'8\")\nGenerous reception room enjoying wonderful natural light, original features and excellent proportions, feature fireplace with cast iron insert and marble hearth - ideal for both entertaining and everyday family use.\n\nHall Floor Return\n\nBathroom - 2.11m (6'11\") x 2.82m (9'3\")\nBath, tiled shower, pedestal whb & wc, fully tiled.\n\nFirst Floor Return\n\nBedroom - 2.11m (6'11\") x 3.05m (10'0\")\nBedroom with cast iron fireplace.\n\nFirst Floor\n\nPrincipal Bedroom - 5.06m (16'7\") x 4.2m (13'9\")\nA magnificent double bedroom, benefitting from superb proportions, high ceilings and ensuite bathroom accommodation.\n\nEn-suite Shower room - 1.31m (4'4\") x 4.2m (13'9\")\nTiled shower, pedestal whb & wc. Wood panelled walls.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.6m (15'1\") x 3.87m (12'8\")\nLarge double bedroom overlooking the rear of the property.\n\nEn-suite Shower room - 1.1m (3'7\") x 2.84m (9'4\")\nTiled shower, pedestal whb & wc. Tiled floor. Wood panelled walls.\n\nSecond Floor Return\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.53m (8'4\") x 4.21m (13'10\")\nA good sized bedroom with excellent natural light and attractive period proportions. Door to en-suite shower room.\n\nEnsuite Shower room - 0.86m (2'10\") x 2.52m (8'3\")\nShower, pedestal whb & wc. Wood panelled walls.\n\nTop Floor Room Suite - 6.37m (20'11\") x 4.57m (15'0\") Max\nAdditional upper-floor accommodation comprising a spacious room together with kitchenette and bathroom facilities, offering excellent flexibility for guests, independent living or home-working requirements.\n\nBathroom - 2.13m (7'0\") x 1.76m (5'9\")\n\nOutside\nRear Garden\nPrivate walled rear garden with patio and seating areas, creating a peaceful outdoor retreat in the heart of Dublin 6. In addition there is a garden shed and outside lighting. \n\nFront Garden \nGated gravelled driveway providing valuable off-street parking, complemented by mature planting and granite steps leading to the main entrance. There is a sun-trap patio area at garden level. \n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
